## Authentication for Protected API Routes

### Where auth happens: `packages/backend/src/auth/macro.ts`

All session validation runs through Elysia plugins defined here. There are two tiers:

**`authPlugin`** (lines 107-117) -- requires a valid session, any role:
```ts
export const authPlugin = new Elysia({ name: "auth-plugin" }).resolve(
  { as: "scoped" },
  async ({ status, request: { headers } }) => {
    const session = await auth.api.getSession({ headers });
    if (!session) return status(401);
    return { user: session.user, session: session.session };
  },
);
```

**`adminPlugin`** (lines 123-141) -- same session check, plus enforces `"admin"` in `user.roles`, else `403`:
```ts
export const adminPlugin = new Elysia({ name: "admin-plugin" }).resolve(
  { as: "scoped" },
  async ({ status, request: { headers } }) => {
    const session = await auth.api.getSession({ headers });
    if (!session) return status(401);
    if (!userRoles?.includes("admin")) return status(403, { error: "..." });
    return { user, session: session.session };
  },
);
```

`auth.api.getSession` is from **Better Auth**, reading the session cookie/token from request headers.

### How a route opts in

A router calls `.use(authPlugin)` or `.use(adminPlugin)` before declaring its routes. The `{ as: "scoped" }` option means the resolved `user` and `session` values are injected into the context of every subsequent route handler on that router only (not globally).

Example from `packages/backend/src/api/admin/detection-patterns.ts:32`:
```ts
export const adminDetectionPatternsRouter = new Elysia({ prefix: "/api/admin/detection-patterns" })
  .use(adminPlugin)   // <-- opts in here; all routes below get auth + admin check
  .get("/", async ({ query }) => { ... })
  .post("/", async ({ body, user }) => { ... })  // user is available from the plugin
```

### Summary

| Plugin | File | Guards |
|---|---|---|
| `authPlugin` | `src/auth/macro.ts:107` | 401 if no session |
| `adminPlugin` | `src/auth/macro.ts:123` | 401 if no session; 403 if not admin |

A router opts in by calling `.use(authPlugin)` or `.use(adminPlugin)` on its Elysia instance. Routes that don't call either plugin are unprotected.

